<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. wheat major net sales activity in the week ended Oct 17 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:    1996/97		   1997/98</p>
<p> Taiwan	  76,900			Nil</p>
<p> Spain	   32,400</p>
<p> Poland	  25,000</p>
<p> Russia	  25,000</p>
<p> Turkey	  23,000</p>
<p> Unknown	-33,600</p>
<p>Net sales of 279,500 tonnes were down 62 percent from the previous week and off 44 percent from the four-week average.</p>
<p>Exports of 591,300 tonnes were up 5 percent from the week earlier, but 17 percent lower than the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary Export Destinations: Egypt (199,500) and Japan (119,000).</p>
</text>
